cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Transept, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Transept: multiobjective, structure-guided multiple sequence alignment of transmembrane proteins"
version: 0.1.0.dev0
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/jMetal/Transept"
abstract: >-
  Transept is a graphical interface for aligning transmembrane proteins with Transept core. It
  guides the user from the datasets, including their own proteins, to runs and their analysis:
  the trade-off alignments, the gaps that break a helix, the agreement with a reference alignment,
  the structures superposed in 3D, and exports to Jalview, ChimeraX and PyMOL.
keywords:
  - multiple sequence alignment
  - transmembrane proteins
  - G protein-coupled receptors
  - multiobjective optimisation
  - AlphaFold2
  - Streamlit
